% Probe: the OTHER consumers of a math sub-run's ink extent, once
% `math_script_drop.saty`'s script shift is right.
%
% `MathGlyph.height`/`.depth` do not only feed `sub_shift_clamped` /
% `sup_shift_clamped`. The same aggregate (`glyphs_extent` /
% `inner_ink_extent`) also sizes a fraction's numerator/denominator raise
% (`math.ml:574-594`), picks a stretchy delimiter's `MathVariants` record
% (`make_paren`, `math.ml:644`, fed `hC`/`dC` — the inner content's ink), and
% then feeds the script clamps AGAIN one level out when the paren itself
% carries a superscript (`h_base` = the paren's own height, so `math.ml:527`'s
% `h_base - SuperscriptBaselineDropMax` candidate can win where a bare letter
% base's never would).
%
% So a wrong ink extent shows up here even when the plain `m_J` script shift
% is correct, and the reverse: this probe must stay flat when
% `math_script_drop.saty` is flat. Rows:
%   1. plain CJK             — the control, must agree exactly
%   2. bare fraction         — numerator/denominator raise off ink extent
%   3. paren'd fraction      — delimiter variant choice off the same extent
%   4. paren + superscript   — the paren's OWN height back into the clamp
@require: stdjabook
@require: math

document (|
  title = {math box extent probe};
  author = {};
  show-title = false;
  show-toc = false;
|) '<
  +p{あいうえお。}
  +p{かきくけこ${\frac{1}{1-v}}さしすせそ。}
  +p{たちつてと${\paren{\frac{1}{1-v}}}なにぬねの。}
  +p{はひふへほ${\paren{\frac{1}{1-v}}^{2}}まみむめも。}
  +p{やゆよ。}
>
